(and end of each header. The output of the parser is a TokenList object, which is a list) Tj T*
(subclass. A TokenList is a recursive data structure. The terminal nodes of the structure are) Tj T*
(Terminal objects, which are subclasses of str. These do not correspond directly to terminal) Tj T*
(objects in the formal grammar, but are instead more practical higher level combinations of) Tj T*
(true terminals. All TokenList and Terminal objects have a 'value' attribute, which produces) Tj T*
(the semantically meaningful value of that part of the parse subtree. The value of all) Tj T*
(whitespace tokens \(no matter how many sub-tokens they may contain\) is a single space, as per) Tj T*
(the RFC rules. This includes 'CFWS', which is herein included in the general class of) Tj T*
(whitespace tokens. There is one exception to the rule that whitespace tokens are collapsed) Tj T*
(into single spaces in values: in the value of a 'bare-quoted-string' \(a quoted-string with) Tj T*
(no leading or trailing whitespace\), any whitespace that appeared between the quotation marks) Tj T*
(is preserved in the returned value. Note that in all Terminal strings quoted pairs are) Tj T*
(turned into their unquoted values.) Tj T*
