(+--------------------+ Note that UnixDatagramServer derives from UDPServer, not from) Tj T*
(UnixStreamServer -- the only difference between an IP and a Unix stream server is the) Tj T*
(address family, which is simply repeated in both unix server classes. To implement a) Tj T*
(service, you must derive a class from BaseRequestHandler and redefine its handle\(\) method.) Tj T*
(You can then run various versions of the service by combining one of the server classes with) Tj T*
(your request handler class. For instance, it makes no sense to use a forking server if the) Tj T*
(service contains state in memory that can be modified by requests \(since the modifications) Tj T*
(in the child process would never reach the initial state kept in the parent process and) Tj T*
(passed to each child\). In this case, you can use a threading server, but you will probably) Tj T*
(have to use locks to avoid two requests that come in nearly simultaneous to apply) Tj T*
(conflicting changes to the server state.) Tj T*
