(to space. A reentrant lock must be released by the thread that acquired it. Once a thread) Tj T*
(has acquired a reentrant lock, the same thread may acquire it again without blocking; the) Tj T*
(thread must release it once for each time it has acquired it. Semaphores manage a counter) Tj T*
(representing the number of release\(\) calls minus the number of acquire\(\) calls, plus an) Tj T*
(initial value. The acquire\(\) method blocks if necessary until it can return without making) Tj T*
(the counter negative. If not given, value defaults to 1. A bounded semaphore checks to make) Tj T*
(sure its current value doesn't exceed its initial value. If it does, ValueError is raised.) Tj T*
(In most situations semaphores are used to guard resources with limited capacity. Like) Tj T*
(regular semaphores, bounded semaphores manage a counter representing the number of release\(\)) Tj T*
(calls minus the number of acquire\(\) calls, plus an initial value. The acquire\(\) method) Tj T*
(blocks if necessary until it can return without making the counter negative. If not given,) Tj T*
