(When invoked with the blocking argument set to false, do not block. If a call without an) Tj T*
(argument would block, return false immediately; otherwise, do the same thing as when called) Tj T*
(without arguments, and return true. When invoked with the floating-point timeout argument) Tj T*
(set to a positive value, block for at most the number of seconds specified by timeout and as) Tj T*
(long as the lock cannot be acquired. Return true if the lock has been acquired, false if the) Tj T*
(timeout has elapsed. If after the decrement it is zero, reset the lock to unlocked \(not) Tj T*
(owned by any thread\), and if any other threads are blocked waiting for the lock to become) Tj T*
(unlocked, allow exactly one of them to proceed. If after the decrement the recursion level) Tj T*
(is still nonzero, the lock remains locked and owned by the calling thread. This method) Tj T*
(releases the underlying lock, and then blocks until it is awakened by a notify\(\) or) Tj T*
(notify_all\(\) call for the same condition variable in another thread, or until the optional) Tj T*
(timeout occurs. Once awakened or timed out, it re-acquires the lock and returns. When the) Tj T*
(underlying lock is an RLock, it is not released using its release\(\) method, since this may) Tj T*
(not actually unlock the lock when it was acquired multiple times recursively. Instead, an) Tj T*
(internal interface of the RLock class is used, which really unlocks it even when it has been) Tj T*
(recursively acquired several times. Another internal interface is then used to restore the) Tj T*
(recursion level when the lock is reacquired. When invoked without arguments: if the internal) Tj T*
(counter is larger than zero on entry, decrement it by one and return immediately. If it is) Tj T*
(zero on entry, block, waiting until some other thread has called release\(\) to make it larger) Tj T*
(than zero. This is done with proper interlocking so that if multiple acquire\(\) calls are) Tj T*
(blocked, release\(\) will wake exactly one of them up. The implementation may pick one at) Tj T*
(random, so the order in which blocked threads are awakened should not be relied on. There is) Tj T*
(no return value in this case.) Tj T*
