(multiple simultaneous dnd processes, e.g. because different button callbacks all) Tj T*
(dnd_start\(\). Potential drag-and-drop targets are discovered as follows. Whenever the mouse) Tj T*
(moves, and at the start and end of a drag-and-drop move, the Tk widget directly under the) Tj T*
(mouse is inspected. This is the target widget \(not to be confused with the target object,) Tj T*
(yet to be determined\). If there is no target widget, there is no dnd target object. If there) Tj T*
(is a target widget, and it has an attribute dnd_accept, this should be a function \(or any) Tj T*
(callable object\). The function is called as dnd_accept\(source, event\), where 'source' is the) Tj T*
(object being dragged \(the object passed to dnd_start\(\) above\), and 'event' is the most) Tj T*
(recent event object \(generally a <Motion> event; it can also be <ButtonPress> or) Tj T*
(<ButtonRelease>\). If the dnd_accept\(\) function returns something other than None, this is) Tj T*
