(The new *maskedarray* is what I eventually come up with. The main differences with the) Tj T*
(initial *numpy.core.ma* package are that MaskedArray is now a subclass of *ndarray* and that) Tj T*
(the *_data* section can now be any subclass of *ndarray*. Apart from a couple of issues) Tj T*
(listed below, the behavior of the new MaskedArray class reproduces the old one. Initially) Tj T*
(the *maskedarray* implementation was marginally slower than *numpy.ma* in some areas, but) Tj T*
(work is underway to speed it up; the expectation is that it can be made substantially faster) Tj T*
(than the present *numpy.ma*. Note that if the subclass has some special methods and) Tj T*
(attributes, they are not propagated to the masked version: this would require a modification) Tj T*
(of the *__getattribute__* method \(first trying *ndarray.__getattribute__*, then trying) Tj T*
(*self._data.__getattribute__* if an exception is raised in the first place\), which really) Tj T*
(slows things down. * The *_data* part of the masked array can be any subclass of ndarray) Tj T*
(\(but not recarray, cf below\). * *fill_value* is now a property, not a function. * in the) Tj T*
(majority of cases, the mask is forced to *nomask* when no value is actually masked. A) Tj T*
(notable exception is when a masked array \(with no masked values\) has just been unpickled. *) Tj T*
(I got rid of the *share_mask* flag, I never understood its purpose. * *put*, *putmask* and) Tj T*
(*take* now mimic the ndarray methods, to avoid unpleasant surprises. Moreover, *put* and) Tj T*
(*putmask* both update the mask when needed. * if *a* is a masked array, *bool\(a\)* raises a) Tj T*
(*ValueError*, as it does with ndarrays. * in the same way, the comparison of two masked) Tj T*
(arrays is a masked array, not a boolean * *filled\(a\)* returns an array of the same subclass) Tj T*
(as *a._data*, and no test is performed on whether it is contiguous or not. * the mask is) Tj T*
(always printed, even if it's *nomask*, which makes things easy \(for me at least\) to remember) Tj T*
(that a masked array is used. * *cumsum* works as if the *_data* array was filled with 0. The) Tj T*
