(Contract Compendium - Section 10) Tj T*
(**Bootstrapping** Currently most popular methods of installing pip rely on pip's self-) Tj T*
(contained nature to install pip itself. These tools work by bundling a copy of pip, adding) Tj T*
(it to ``sys.path``, and then executing that copy of pip. This is done instead of) Tj T*
(implementing a "mini installer" \(to reduce duplication\); pip already knows how to install a) Tj T*
(Python package, and is far more battle-tested than any "mini installer" could ever possibly) Tj T*
(be. Many downstream redistributors have policies against this kind of bundling, and instead) Tj T*
(opt to patch the software they distribute to debundle it and make it rely on the global) Tj T*
(versions of the software that they already have packaged \(which may have its own patches) Tj T*
(applied to it\). We \(the pip team\) would prefer it if pip was *not* debundled in this manner) Tj T*
(due to the above reasons and instead we would prefer it if pip would be left intact as it is) Tj T*
(now. In the longer term, if someone has a *portable* solution to the above problems, other) Tj T*
(than the bundling method we currently use, that doesn't add additional problems that are) Tj T*
(unreasonable then we would be happy to consider, and possibly switch to said method. This) Tj T*
(solution must function correctly across all of the situation that we expect pip to be used) Tj T*
(and not mandate some external mechanism such as OS packages. * ``setuptools`` is completely) Tj T*
(stripped to only keep ``pkg_resources``. * ``pkg_resources`` has been modified to import its) Tj T*
(dependencies from ``pip._vendor``, and to use the vendored copy of ``platformdirs`` rather) Tj T*
(than ``appdirs``. * ``packaging`` has been modified to import its dependencies from) Tj T*
(``pip._vendor``. * ``CacheControl`` has been modified to import its dependencies from) Tj T*
(``pip._vendor``. * ``requests`` has been modified to import its other dependencies from) Tj T*
(``pip._vendor`` and to *not* load ``simplejson`` \(all platforms\) and ``pyopenssl``) Tj T*
(\(Windows\). * ``rich`` has been modified to load Unicode tables from its vendored namespace.) Tj T*
(* ``platformdirs`` has been modified to import its submodules from) Tj T*
(``pip._vendor.platformdirs``.) Tj T*
(Page 379) Tj T*
