(bundled `websockets` dependency. If `websockets` is not > available, `run\(\)` falls back to) Tj T*
(HTTP, which has its own request-level > timeout. After a command finishes \(exits\), its) Tj T*
(session remains in memory for a TTL period. During this window you can still reconnect to) Tj T*
(retrieve output. After the TTL expires, the session is cleaned up and `reconnect\(\)` will) Tj T*
(raise an error. Running commands with no connected clients are killed after an idle timeout) Tj T*
(\(default: 5 minutes\). The idle timer resets each time a client connects. This prevents) Tj T*
(orphaned long-running processes from consuming resources indefinitely. ```python with) Tj T*
(client.sandbox\(snapshot_id=snapshot_id\) as sb: # Start a long-running command with a) Tj T*
(30-minute idle timeout handle = sb.run\( "python server.py", timeout=0, idle_timeout=1800,) Tj T*
(wait=False, \) ```python with client.sandbox\(snapshot_id=snapshot_id\) as sb: # Long-running) Tj T*
(task: 30-min idle timeout, 1-hour session TTL handle = sb.run\( "python train.py", timeout=0,) Tj T*
